[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue, on subject lines alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Read by tenant, form and body, the
reports hold three problems. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 fixes only the first row. The other two stay broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day first,
  so day and month swap: 7 May lands on 5 July.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the
  hint says, and the form reads it day first. Fixing the parser does not touch this; the hint must change.
- **`shift`**: the date moves by one day, not a swap. The same meeting shows Tuesday in Lisbon and
  Monday in Toronto. A time zone bug. The desk already listed these reports as one-day moves in
  `desk-notes.json`; the old table still counts them under `parser`.

## How the reports were counted

- The ticket export repeats some rows across its pages; each report id counts once.
- A report is placed by its tenant and the way it came in, not by its intake tag. Intake tags
  `hint` on every report from a US-English browser, which says nothing about the cause.

## Lessons

- Same subject is not same problem. Read a sample of bodies before calling a big ticket known.
- Count by cause, and file one ticket per cause.

